  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "This report studies quantum accelerated Monte Carlo for derivative pricing and VaR using amplitude estimation on a Black-Scholes model discretized with 5 qubits over 32 intervals on [0.01, 5.0]. The experiments compare CQPEAE, IQPEAE, IQAE, MLAE, and RQAE on simulator/compute-node environments (QLM and FT3), showing quadratic error scaling in theory, but the authors explicitly state the methods are not yet competitive on NISQ hardware and that the new encoding introduces a large Npaths factor.",
